    description: "After the import-target fixes (proto, Thrift, Cap'n Proto, Make, requirements, Terraform, Ruby require_relative), these forms still do not reach the file node that is in the tree:\n- make: \"include $(VAR)/x.mk\" emits no edge.\n- perl: require \"lib.pl\"; emits no edge.\n- ruby: a plain require is not looked up along the load path (lib/ of the gem).\n- tcl: a \"namespace import\" written in another file is not read by the call resolver.\n- Vue/Svelte/Astro component imports: aliases other than @/ ($lib/, ~/, @components/) are not resolved; js-module-linker does not run on a tree that has only .svelte/.vue files (its gate needs javascript/typescript), so <script> imports there stay unresolved.\n- firejail profile .inc files open with \"include x.local\" and are still classified BitBake (0 nodes; the pass reads them).\n- tsconfig references (WI-husim, open): the edge ends on a stand-in at the raw reference path (json:./pkg/tsconfig.json:0-0:tsconfig.json:external_symbol) although pkg/tsconfig.json is a file node in the tree; a directory reference (./pkg) is not looked up either. Same on dev before and after the id fixes.\nRepros: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/idfive_11232026/analyzers/RESULTS.md, sfc/RESULTS.md.\nEvidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/idfive_11232026/ (STATUS.md, <package>/RESULTS.md, bump/report_run2.txt). Found 2026-11-23 while building WI-funip, WI-supar, WI-sagur, WI-jozih and WI-sidus."  # 58c6
